<h1>Thanos Sort</h1>
<p>
    Thanos Sort begins by checking if the array is sorted.
    If it is not sorted it removes half of the array elements at random.
    It repeats this process until the array is sorted.
    This usually results in only a couple of elements being left over from the original array.
    <br><br>
    Each time Thanos Sort removes an element, all elements afterwards must be shifted to fill the empty space.
    Since Thanos Sort typically removes most of the array, this results in it
    having an average and worst Time Complexity of <b>n<sup>2</sup></b>.
</p>

